WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.820
Star Wars fans are thrilled that Jacen Syndulla&nbsp;
might walk the path of the Jedi — but the latest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:10.140
Ahsoka episode suggests that things could&nbsp;
be about to get very dark, very quickly.

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:15.720
Ahsoka Tano is in a pickle. After being thoroughly&nbsp;
defeated by Baylan Skoll in the previous episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.460
she spends the majority of Ahsoka's fifth part&nbsp;
trapped in the Force limbo known as the World&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:24.960
Between Worlds. Her experience there involves&nbsp;
multiple flashbacks to the war-torn days of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.860
her youth, as well as a ghostly vision&nbsp;
of her old master, Anakin Skywalker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:33.960
who uses some characteristically aggressive&nbsp;
methods to complete his former Padawan's training.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:38.160
Back in the physical world, Ahsoka's allies&nbsp;
struggle to track her down — and, once again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.600
strange Force antics end up saving&nbsp;
the day. Hera Syndulla's son, Jacen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:47.040
uses an impressive and clearly Force-enhanced&nbsp;
listening skill to get an idea of Ahsoka's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.613
whereabouts, as he hears snippets of her&nbsp;
experience in the World Between Worlds.

00:00:51.146 --> 00:00:52.526
"Don't you hear it?"

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:58.740
Known as Theran Force-listening, this ability&nbsp;
allows Force-users to hear things from great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:03.660
distances. This power also has other handy&nbsp;
applications, such as allowing the user to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:07.920
understand other languages. While not exactly&nbsp;
common in the live-action Star Wars universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:12.060
many prominent Jedi characters have mastered&nbsp;
the trick in various "Legends" works.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:16.200
The show's choice to give Jacen Theran&nbsp;
Force-listening abilities is particularly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:21.360
interesting, as the skill is closely associated&nbsp;
with a similarly-named character from an extremely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:26.580
dead corner of the Star Wars lore: Jacen&nbsp;
Solo, the son of Han Solo and Leia Organa.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:31.320
In many ways, Jacen Solo is a scarier&nbsp;
Star Wars villain than Darth Vader. A&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:35.400
prominent character in non-canon Star Wars&nbsp;
novels, he starts out as a perfectly capable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:40.680
Force-sensitive kid who eventually becomes a&nbsp;
powerful and respected hero. Unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:42.660
the plot of the books puts him through the kind of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:46.200
wringer that would make his live-action&nbsp;
successor, Kylo Ren, run for the hills.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:50.400
Jacen's path ultimately takes an&nbsp;
unfortunate turn, and unlike Kylo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:56.220
he goes all in on the Dark Side. As the Sith Lord&nbsp;
Darth Caedus, Jacen becomes something of a tragic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:01.860
villain... but also a true terror who, among other&nbsp;
things, kills Luke Skywalker's wife, Mara Jade.

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:05.760
Any "Legends" fan will tell you that Darth&nbsp;
Caedus is one of the most overpowered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:10.080
antagonists in the entire franchise, with a&nbsp;
laundry list of Force superpowers that put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:13.800
him almost on par with Luke himself.&nbsp;
He's also notorious for picking up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:18.060
some of the stranger Force skills out there —&nbsp;
including, of course, Theran Force-listening.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:22.380
Since the live-action Star Wars universe has&nbsp;
pretty much overwritten Jacen by establishing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:26.730
Kylo Ren as Han and Leia's only son, it's&nbsp;
highly unlikely that he'll become canon any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:30.840
time soon. Nevertheless, fans will have noticed&nbsp;
that Ahsoka chose to give one of his most famous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:35.940
Force abilities to a kid with the same name — and&nbsp;
might see it as a red flag for Syndulla's future.

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:40.560
So what could go wrong? Well, as Kanan&nbsp;
Jarrus' son, Jacen has the potential to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:45.360
a truly powerful Force user. The fact that he's&nbsp;
able to use a rare and obscure Jedi skill like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:50.760
Theran Force-listening with no training suggests a&nbsp;
natural affinity with the Force. And the fact that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:54.240
he's able to hear what's going on in the World&nbsp;
Between Worlds might hint at a level of power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:59.220
approaching that of Jacen Solo. Since Jacen is&nbsp;
effectively out of the canon picture and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:03.780
younger Jacen's story is largely unwritten, could&nbsp;
the fact that he has access to a similar Force&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:08.700
ability be an ominous hint that he's destined to&nbsp;
follow a similar path? It's hard to say for sure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:12.660
but Ahsoka fans will want to keep a close eye&nbsp;
on the young Syndulla as the series draws on.

